# Code owners.
#
# NOTE ON ENFORCEMENT: this file only gates anything if branch protection on
# `main` has "Require review from Code Owners" enabled. Without that it is
# documentation. The entries below are written assuming it will be turned on;
# until it is, treat them as intent rather than as a control.
#
# Path granularity is CODEOWNERS' only namespace, so semantic ownership is
# obtained the established way (api-extractor, buf breaking, golden files):
# project the semantic object into a file, gate drift in CI, own the file.
# See scripts/schema-export.ts and .github/workflows/schema-drift.yml.

# The mirror's schema — both the hand-written intent and the generated
# projection of what is actually deployed. Owning this directory means every
# change to the deployed queue schema surfaces as a diff requiring review,
# regardless of which source file (or which out-of-band `dolt sql`) caused it.
# The S1 bug lived in the gap this closes: the tables existed only in the
# database, so there was nothing for anyone to review.
/schema/ @bdelanghe

# The projector and its gate. If these can be changed without review, the
# ownership above is unenforceable — a weakened check silently un-owns /schema/.
/scripts/schema-export.ts        @bdelanghe
/.github/workflows/schema-drift.yml @bdelanghe

# Ownership of ownership.
/.github/CODEOWNERS @bdelanghe

# The verified specs. Changes here alter what "proven" means for this repo.
/specs/ @bdelanghe
